    "established_connections": [
      "Persist-before-compute gives one executed generation and encapsulation origin per authoritative local epoch.",
      "Eligible executed-slot source-association failure implies a signature event stopped before target-key/file return or a framed-input hash collision.",
      "Exact signature component adapters preserve original reservation randomizers, query ledgers, owner indices and replay. The classical native deterministic P-256 bound has an explicit U single-user conversion.",
      "A generic signing construction separates ordinary unforgeability from the interface exposing the original signing randomizer."
    ],
    "attribution_bound": "eta_attr^exec <= min(1, epsilon_sig + chi_H(Q_H))",
    "declared_instantiation": "The post-quantum branch uses the named reservation-aware ML-DSA assumption; the classical branch uses the actual deterministic RFC6979 P-256 signing distribution.",
    "controller_hypothesis": "One authoritative history per admitted endpoint/session/epoch. A two-live-journal countermodel documents why this is substantive.",
    "owner_interface": "Public owner metadata and exact signing reservations; stopped before a target signing-key/seed-file return, with no earlier byte-dependent observation of that secret owner file."
  },
